  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Features\n\nIndexer keys of a custom ref struct type (#297, part of #201). A key of a ref struct type, passed by value, no longer reports IMP009. An imposter can't keep or match a ref struct key, so it passes the key through:\n\nSetups and verification match the other keys only, as in imposter\\[Arg\\<int>.Any()].Getter().Returns((row, locator) => row + locator.Offset).\n\nThe delegates passed to Returns, Callback and Throws, and the base implementation, get the key.\n\nThe default behaviour keeps a value set by the other keys, whatever the ref struct key.\n\nAn indexer whose keys are all ref structs, or whose other keys are another indexer's, is set up by a method named after it, such as imposter.Indexer() or imposter.Indexer\\_1(). Its interface's setup view declares the same method.\n\nStill IMP009 (see Limitations):\n\na ref struct indexer key taken by in;\n\na class indexer of a ref struct type with an in or ref readonly key and a base getter;\n\na ref struct whose type uses a method's type parameters;\n\na ref struct argument of an async event;\n\ntype parameters that allow ref structs;\n\na span returned by reference.",
